Additional Terms for EE ZONE Platform

1. Attribution Requirement
   Any public deployment or fork of this software must visibly credit the
   original author: Ajinkya Chalke (ajinkyachalke008@gmail.com) in the
   application UI, documentation, or README.

2. Non-Commercial AI Use
   The AI-powered features of this platform (Instrument Scanner, Problem
   Solver, AI Circuit Designer, AI Code Assistant, AI Troubleshooter) are
   intended for educational and engineering purposes. Commercial resale of
   these AI features as a standalone product is not permitted without
   explicit written permission from the author.

3. Educational Use Encouraged
   Students, educators, and academic institutions are explicitly encouraged
   to use, fork, and adapt this platform for non-commercial educational
   purposes. No permission needed — just keep the attribution.

4. Contributions
   Contributions via pull requests are welcome. By submitting a contribution,
   you agree that your code will be licensed under this same MIT License and
   that copyright of the contribution is shared with the project author.

5. No Warranty on Electrical Calculations
   The engineering calculators, simulations, and compliance tools in this
   platform are provided for reference and educational purposes only. They
   should NOT be used as the sole basis for real-world electrical installations
   or safety-critical decisions. Always verify results with a licensed
   professional engineer.

